<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain your reasoning. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para><emphasis>Strategy 1: Solve for \(y\).</emphasis></para>
    <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Subtract the \(x\) term from both sides.</para>
    <para><emphasis>Step 2 </emphasis>- Simplify.</para>
    <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Divide both sides by the coefficient of \(y\).</para>
    <para><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Simplify.<emphasis>Strategy 2: Use standard form. </emphasis>
    </para>
